"Licence" means a licence to use Spacetile that you bought from Kodehort or
that Kodehort granted to you, used under the Spacetile End User Licence
Agreement at https://spacetile.app/eula/ (the "EULA").

"Licence key" means the token that proves a Licence to the app.

"Trial" means the period the EULA allows Spacetile to be used without a
Licence.

"Licence check" means the code in the Software that tracks the Trial,
verifies Licence keys and stops features when neither applies.

"Development build" means a build of the Software made with
`scripts/bundle.sh --dev`, which leaves the Licence check out.


2. What you may do without a Licence

Kodehort grants you a personal, worldwide, non-exclusive, non-transferable,
royalty-free licence, which ends as section 7 describes, to:

  (a) read and audit the Software;

  (b) make Development builds and run them on Macs you control, only to study
      how the Software works, check its behaviour or security, or investigate
      and report a problem with it; and

  (c) modify the Software for the purposes in (b).


3. Every other use needs a Licence

Any other use of the Software is allowed only under the EULA, which needs a
Licence once the Trial it offers has ended. That includes running a
Development build for everyday work and running any build other than a
Development build.


